{"availability":"available","full":"Jamil1016/drmc-demo","name":"drmc-demo","description":"Workforce report compliance app: approvals with durable bulk approve, hours analysis. Demo data only.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-20T01:16:13Z","updated":"2026-09-20T03:48:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://drmc-demo.vercel.app","topics":["dashboard","nextjs","playwright","postgres","supabase","typescript"],"demo":"https://drmc-demo.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:08:13.527Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:08:13.527Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:08:13.527Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:08:13.527Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DRMC is a workforce report-compliance app. People file a daily report of the hours they worked; team leads approve those reports in a project-management system; managers need to see who is on the roster, what is waiting for approval, how fast it gets approved, and whether the hours people state match the hours their timers recorded. This repository is a working copy of that app that anyone can run and click through.","This is a sanitized public demo of DRMC, an internal workforce report-compliance platform I designed and built. It contains a slice of the real application (directory, approvals with durable bulk approve, DR monitoring, hours analysis, activity log) running in a permanent demo mode. Every person, team, client and number is invented, policy thresholds have been changed, integrations are simulated, and the features that encode HR policy or send email have been removed.","Stack: Next.js 16 (App Router, server components and server actions), React 19, Supabase (Postgres + Auth), Tailwind CSS 4, TypeScript."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jamil1016/drmc-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3162da6a4e2aa109975596d3182779cd24d